<!--
    NodeProgressIcon – the 16 × 16 square progress mark of a node (Paper "9c · Running", node tabs;
    drawn large on "14 · Node status icons", section "squircle pie").

        ╭──────╮      ╭──────╮      ╭──────╮      ╭──────╮      ╭──────╮●     ████████
        │      │      │   ▗▄ │      │   █▌ │      │ ▄▄█▌ │      │   █▌ │      ██ ✓ ███
        │      │      │      │      │   █▌ │      │ ▀▀█▌ │      │   █▌ │      ████████
        ╰──────╯      ╰──────╯      ╰──────╯      ╰──────╯      ╰──────╯
        waiting        25 %          50 %          75 %        with a problem    done

    Parts, back to front, all in a 16-unit box:
      1. Outline ... rounded square, 1.5 stroke, outer edge from 1.25 to 14.75, corner radius 4.95.
      2. Fill ...... a smaller rounded square (3.9 … 12.1, radius 2.4), 1.15 away from the outline. It is always
                     the full shape; a pie-shaped clip that opens clockwise from 12 o'clock reveals as much of it as
                     the node has finished. So any value works – 48 % is not rounded to a half.
      3. Done ...... solid green rounded square + white check, shown once every test of the node ran.
      4. Dot ....... badge on the top-right corner: red after a failure, amber after an abort (red wins).
                     It has a 1.3 ring in the colour of the surface behind the icon, so it reads as "cut out".

    Colours come from outside, so one control serves the selected tab, the idle tabs and the single-mode header:
      Foreground ... outline + fill          (blue on the selected tab, grey on the others)
      DotRing ...... ring around the dot     (the tab's background colour)

    Motion (NodeProgressIcon.xaml.cs):
      · progress ..... the clip sweeps smoothly to the new value instead of jumping
      · done ......... outline and fill fade out while the green square fades in; the check then draws itself
      · dot .......... fades in and settles from 80 % to full size the first time a problem shows up
    Nothing grows out of a point, and with Windows animations turned off every change is immediate.

    Use:  <local:NodeProgressIcon Progress="{Binding Fraction}" IsComplete="{Binding IsComplete}"
                                  HasFailed="{Binding HasFailed}" HasAborted="{Binding HasAborted}"
                                  Foreground="{StaticResource Blue}" DotRing="{StaticResource White}" />
-->
<UserControl x:Class="Conduit.NodeProgressIcon"
             x:Name="Root"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             Width="16" Height="16"
             Focusable="False"
             VerticalAlignment="Center">

    <Canvas Width="16" Height="16">

        <!-- 1 · Outline -->
        <Rectangle x:Name="Outline" Canvas.Left="1.25" Canvas.Top="1.25" Width="13.5" Height="13.5"
                   RadiusX="4.95" RadiusY="4.95" StrokeThickness="1.5"
                   Stroke="{Binding Foreground, ElementName=Root}" />

        <!-- 2 · Fill: the whole inner shape. Its Clip (a pie slice around the shape's centre) is set by the code-behind. -->
        <Rectangle x:Name="Fill" Canvas.Left="3.9" Canvas.Top="3.9" Width="8.2" Height="8.2"
                   RadiusX="2.4" RadiusY="2.4"
                   Fill="{Binding Foreground, ElementName=Root}" />

        <!-- 3 · Done: green square + check. The check is a stroke, so it can be drawn along its path. -->
        <Rectangle x:Name="DoneFill" Canvas.Left="1.25" Canvas.Top="1.25" Width="13.5" Height="13.5"
                   RadiusX="4.9" RadiusY="4.9" Fill="{StaticResource Green}" Opacity="0" />
        <Path x:Name="DoneCheck" Data="M4.9,8.2 L7,10.3 L11.1,6.1" Stroke="White" StrokeThickness="1.7"
              StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" StrokeLineJoin="Round" Opacity="0" />

        <!-- 4 · Dot: centre (13.2, 2.8), radius 2.6 plus the 1.3 ring → a 6.5 px ellipse. Fill is set in code. -->
        <Ellipse x:Name="Dot" Canvas.Left="9.95" Canvas.Top="-0.45" Width="6.5" Height="6.5"
                 StrokeThickness="1.3" Opacity="0" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5"
                 Stroke="{Binding DotRing, ElementName=Root}">
            <Ellipse.RenderTransform>
                <ScaleTransform x:Name="DotScale" />
            </Ellipse.RenderTransform>
        </Ellipse>
    </Canvas>
</UserControl>
